          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धीरे (dhīre) — \"slowly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit धीर (dhīra), which meant steady, calm, firm of mind. Hindi's word for slow is the old word for unhurried, and the compliment inside it never quite left."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Doubled — धीरे (dhīre) धीरे (dhīre) — it means 'little by little', and that doubled form is the one you will hear most. Saying a word twice to mean a gentle continuing is one of the most useful habits Hindi has."
            }
          ]
        },
