          "title": "You'll want to know: कम",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कम (kam) — \"little, not much\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Persian kam, 'few, little', taken in whole. It answers 'how much' with a shrug downward, and it can sit in front of almost anything a speaker wants to play down."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One warning, and it is about our letters rather than about Hindi. कमरा, the room you learnt in the house arc, begins with the same two sounds and has nothing whatever to do with कम — it walked in from Portuguese. In Devanagari nobody would confuse them; in a romanization kam and kamrā sit uncomfortably close."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
