        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ज़्यादा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ज़्यादा (zyādā) — \"a lot, more\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arabic زيادة (ziyāda), 'an increase', through Persian. It is the exact counterweight of कम (kam), and the two of them are the fastest way in Hindi to answer 'how much' without naming a number."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The nukta under the ज़ is doing real work, the same as in ज़रूर. Drop it and you have a different consonant; keep it and you have the sound Persian and Arabic brought with the word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: अब (ab), जल्दी (jaldī), धीरे (dhīre), कम (kam), ज़्यादा (zyādā). Enough to answer how much and how fast."
            }
          ]
        },
